{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"KEY DESIGN DECISIONS (and who made them)\n\n1. Fold 1803 into jira-reb-1582 rather than fix separately — 1803 was a symptom of the type-tier policy, not an independent defect. Operator choice.\n2. Escalate cousins per the 1582 spec. Two leaves in different sub-trees now escalate to their parents where they previously linked directly. Operator choice, taken knowingly: it inverted three existing tests while eight held unchanged, which was the main evidence the formulation was right.\n3. A standalone `link-audit` verb REJECTED for core — rebar already had three detect-and-remediate surfaces (fsck --repair, validate --fix, this) with two different \"fix it\" flag names. Became `rebar doctor`s first check, framed as a named check list so later checks slot in without new verbs. Operator direction.\n4. Fail OPEN on the retype fix rather than invalidate every attestation. Operator direction, and correct: adding ticket_type to the material fingerprint would have invalidated every certified ticket AND broken two hardcoded fingerprint SHAs at tests/unit/test_plan_review.py:1023-1024. The sidecar already recorded ticket_type, so the fail-open compare needed no schema change.\n5. Do NOT remove quiet=True to fix the MCP silence. rebar-mcp speaks MCP-over-stdio; an unsuppressed print inside a tool call would inject a bare JSON object into the JSON-RPC stream. The defect was that stdout was the ONLY channel, not that it is suppressed — so the record became a return value.\n\nEVIDENCE THAT MATTERED\n- The retype defect is consequential, not theoretical: on scratch ticket cf19-d1e0-e817-4510 the SAME plan BLOCKs as a task and PASSes as a bug, because bug is exempt from criteria task is not.\n- The store DRIFTS on its own: after remediating to zero scheduling-affecting findings, two NEW mis-escalated edges with OPEN endpoints appeared within hours. Re-parenting silently invalidates previously-correct links because comparability is structural."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785448745529302001,"uuid":"bd0b4811-cf3b-4e53-91eb-d83984e0f7c2"}